&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures&lt;/strong&gt;: All photos and video recordings of SCP-5502 are to be confiscated and archived. Witnesses of SCP-5502 events are to be administered amnestics before release. Mobile Task Force Omicron-17 (&amp;quot;Go for the gold&amp;quot;) is dedicated to capturing the SCP-5502-1 instances. The captured SCP-5502-1 instances are to be contained in separate containment chambers at Site-228.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description&lt;/strong&gt;: SCP-5502 is an event which occurs at a random time and location, and starts with the manifestation of an approximately 15-25 centimeter tall humanoid entity whose body is composed of solid gold, hereafter referred to as SCP-5502-1. SCP-5502-1 typically manifests in the vicinity of large groups, in which it will begin to run at 40&amp;#160;km/h, in the opposite direction the group faces. The people in the group, hereafter referred to as SCP-5502-2, will begin to chase SCP-5502-1. If a member of SCP-5502-2 succeeds in capturing SCP-5502-1, it will start to consume the entity. Despite SCP-5502-1 being made of solid gold, the SCP-5502-2 member will have no difficulties consuming it (aside from SCP-5502-1&#039;s attempts to escape). The aforementioned SCP-5502-2 instance will then receive an amount of money equal to that of the gold in an SCP-5502-1&#039;s body within the next 10-12 hours. After SCP-5502-1 escapes or is consumed, all members of SCP-5502-2 forget the events since SCP-5502-1&#039;s manifestation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only those individuals who were in the vicinity of SCP-5502-1&#039;s initial manifestation can become a member of SCP-5502-2. If SCP-5502-1 encounters any other individuals following initial manifestation, they usually will not make any attempt to chase or consume SCP-5502-1. The only known evidence of SCP-5502&#039;s existence are video recordings by surveillance cameras, as well as eyewitnesses of the event.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Currently, 132 SCP-5502 events are known to have occurred since 1980, and 35 SCP-5502-1 instances are under Foundation custody. The contained entities do not try to communicate with Foundation personnel or to breach containment. Instead, these run around their containment chambers in the opposite direction of the nearest human.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Notable SCP-5502-1 manifestations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;wiki-content-table&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5502-1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Place of manifestation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Status&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;20 centimeters tall morbidly obese male humanoid&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;In a bariatric clinic&#039;s lobby&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Contained&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;21 centimeters tall male humanoid in a prison guard uniform&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;During a prison riot in France&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Consumed by SCP-5502-2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;17 centimeters tall female humanoid with four arms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;During a mass praying in India&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Contained&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;23 centimeters tall male humanoid whose features are similar to the actor and comedian Jim Carrey&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;In a movie theater during the premiere of &amp;quot;The Number 23&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Contained&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;22 centimeters tall male humanoid in a tuxedo&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;In a shopping center during Black Friday&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Consumed by SCP-5502-2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum:&lt;/strong&gt; In 2010, an envelope manifested on the floor near the containment unit of the SCP-5502-1 instances. The envelope contained the following message:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;float: center; border: solid 3px #444444; width: 85%; padding: 1px 15px; margin: auto; margin-top: 10px; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.2);&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For all the members of the Foundation,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thank you very much for being a part of this game for so long. I can&#039;t believe that. When I started the first contest thirty years ago I thought it will be a failure but these thirty years and you guys proved me wrong. I can&#039;t believe you guys were able to catch thirty-five without eating them. All of you earned my respect by proving that playing and having fun is the most important part of the game and not the reward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I hope we can continue this for at least another thirty years or more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
