&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BEGIN LOG&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;02/05/200█&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5176-1 has been enticed into aquarium containment with 64 live tuna. Head Researcher Dr. Chambers begins interviewing SCP-5176-1 though a Portuguese translator. Document has been wholly translated.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; Hello, SCP-5176-1. Can you hear me?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5176-1 proceeds to continue luring and consuming fish, while raising a pseudopod to write an answer on the aquarium glass in fine print&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: Hello. I hear you. I like your fish.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; You may have as many as you&#039;d like. I&#039;m going to ask you some questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: When I eat fish I happy. If I happy I do questions. You give fish. Good?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Dr. Edmund&#039;s orders the addition of 20 tuna into the enclosure.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; Thank you for your cooperation. How do you know Portuguese?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: Learned it.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; from whom?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: From long lungfish shepherds.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Aside.&lt;/em&gt; Are you sure you&#039;re translating that right? The hell does that mean? &lt;em&gt;Into the microphone.&lt;/em&gt; Ok, let&#039;s move on. What are you?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: My name [untranslatable]&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-989328-7&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Aside&lt;/em&gt;. Hm. A name. Unexpected. Are we getting this all down before the ink comes off the glass? Excellent. &lt;em&gt;Into the microphone.&lt;/em&gt; Well, err&amp;#8230; I&#039;m going to call you SCP-5176-1. What are you?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: I [untranslatable]. I like fish.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; Well, I can see that. Are you made of octopuses?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: I think you not see me. Only see tips.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; Tips? Tips of what?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: More fish.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Dr. Chambers orders staff to dump the remaining 20 tuna into the enclosure&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: It is like big smooth loud fish. When it swim on water, I only see tip. But, much more is there. I am like that. You only see tips.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Aside.&lt;/em&gt; I think it&#039;s talking dimensionally. &lt;em&gt;Into the microphone.&lt;/em&gt; What tips are we seeing? What are you really like?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5176-1 finishes consuming the enclosed tuna and suddenly presses its bulk against the glass.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; Jesus&amp;#8230; Christ.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5176-1 teleports to an unknown location, leaving behind a cavity of air that collapses loudly. There is writing left behind on the glass&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: &lt;em&gt;Long lungfishes don&#039;t have many fish. I come back when give many fish.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;sub&gt;Your fish tasty&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;END LOG&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Researcher&#039;s Note:&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Log-5176-A1-02/05/200█ clearly indicates that SCP-5176-1 possesses complete or almost-&lt;br /&gt;
complete sapience, and should always be treated as such. In addition, SCP-5176-1&#039;s description of its form indicates that SCP-5176 may be the corporeal appendages of a much larger&lt;br /&gt;
transdimensional being or beings. This would explain the teleportation and affection of DPK levels.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Further interview attempts requested in order to determine and confirm the exact nature of SCP-&amp;gt; 5176-1 and what the hell it means when it talks.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;-Dr. Reese Chambers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Approved.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;-Site-██ Director ██████&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;Interview&amp;nbsp;Log-5176-A2-02/20/200█&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;Access&amp;nbsp;Granted&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BEGIN LOG&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;02/20/200█&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5176-1 has been enticed into containment with the use of 85 tuna and six specimens of Blacktip reef shark. Dr. Edmund confirms that the entity is the same spoken with in Log-5176-A1.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; So, SCP-5176-1, last time we spoke, you said I could only see your tips.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: &lt;sub&gt;fish&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; Hm. What did you mean by that? What part of you is hidden?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: Big thing. Filled with hooks.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; Filled with hooks? Like a fishing boat?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: Big hooks. Hooks need fish.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; Can you describe this part of yourself any further?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: Big water. Sometimes the waves get tall and there are fish in them. Then I reach up and taste the fish. You see tips. I am deep.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; How&amp;#8230;deep?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5176-1 finishes feeding and pulses blue. It then presses its mass against the aquarium glass and de-manifests. There is a complicated glyph left behind in ink.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;END LOG&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Researcher&#039;s Note:&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;The glyph photographed following Interview-5176-A2 consists of concentric circles of points, alternating with symbols roughly analogous to slashes(/), plus and minus signs(+, -), as well as two symbols of unknown significance. It will hereby be referred to as SCP-5176-2.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5176-2 and its associated photographs have also displayed mild cognitohazardous effects. Subjects exposed to SCP-5176-2 report unnatural feelings of unease, and many suffer from attacks of &amp;gt; thalassophobia&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-989328-8&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;. Thalassophobic attacks appear in subjects with no history of the phobia and can occur in any setting, irrespective of proximity to the ocean.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Inexplicably, in the process of testing the memetic effect of SCP-6176-2, it has been ascertained that approximately 8% of subjects react much more strongly than is standard. In this group, exposure to SCP-5176-2 results in bouts of obsessive behavior. This primarily takes the form of the compulsive creation of poetry and prose regarding SCP-5176-2, although on one occasion a stage play involving SCP-5176-2 was produced. These works have no anomalous properties and contain no data of use.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;It has been hypothesized that SCP-5176-2 represents an encoded message, although the meaning of the pattern&#039;s placement and nomenclature is currently unclear. Further analysis recommended.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;-Head Researcher Dr. Reese Chambers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;Addendum&amp;nbsp;1:&amp;nbsp;SCP-5176-2&amp;nbsp;Analysis&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;Access&amp;nbsp;Granted&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5176-2 has been analyzed using SCP-████ and machine learning. SCP-5176-2 has been discovered to relate to traditional binary code, however it is also augmented with █████ code. When &amp;gt; deciphered, it is roughly analogous to the non-anomalous astrophysical formula publicly known as &amp;gt; the Friedman equation&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-989328-9&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;. There is additional information that appears to be a probable solution to the so-called &amp;quot;Cuspy Halo Problem&amp;quot;, a previously unsolved discrepancy in the dark matter density observed in small galaxies when compared to N-body simulations. The proof displays that CDM halos posses &amp;quot;cusps&amp;quot; of matter that account for the discrepancies.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Foundation physicists have proposed a new hypothesis regarding SCP-5176 using the additional information provided by SCP-5176-2. It is theoretically possible that it might inhabit or constitute dark matter, and is manifesting as an organism for an unknown reason. This would explain the effect &amp;gt; on local DPK levels as well as its current method of teleportation. In addition, Foundation physicists &amp;gt; have proposed a method by which dark matter could hypothetically fluctuate DPK levels fast enough to alter neurochemistry and produce a memetic effect like that exhibited by SCP-5176. This model is consistent with DPK readings observed during interview sessions. Going forward, it is recommended that Head Researcher Dr. Chambers approach SCP-5176-1 with extreme caution. Dark &amp;gt; matter constitutes 80% of known matter in the non-anomalous universe.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;-████ ████████, Administrator, Lab ANA-6&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Researcher&#039;s Note:&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Permission to experiment with the use of full-phase local DPK fields via ██████ generator in order to contain SCP-5176-1.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;-Head Researcher Dr. Reese Chambers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Approved. Proceed with caution.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;-Site-██ Director ██████&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;Interview&amp;nbsp;Log-5176-A3-04/05/200█&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;Access&amp;nbsp;Granted&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;BEGIN LOG&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;04/05/200█&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;A Full-phase DPK ██████ generator has been placed into the aquarium prior to SCP-5176-1&#039;s arrival. The ██████ generator has been deactivated and placed on switch trigger. Chambers hopes to contain SCP-5176-1 or force it to reveal itself. SCP-5176-1 has been enticed with the use of ten blacktip reef sharks and roughly 150 tuna.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5176-1, why do you respond to fish specifically?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: &lt;sub&gt;I like fish&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Please&lt;/em&gt;, 5176-1. I need you to elaborate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5176-1 draws a glyph on the glass.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: fish taste like this&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-989328-10&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Aside.&lt;/em&gt; Did we get that down? Good. Keep the ██████ generator hot. &lt;em&gt;On mic.&lt;/em&gt; Would you be willing to remain in containment and receive as many fish as you like, daily?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5176-1: Can&#039;t. Only tips here. I am deep.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Chambers:&lt;/strong&gt; Well, we&#039;ll see about that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The ██████ generator is activated, pushing DPK levels to full-phase in the aquarium. SCP-5176-1 pulses blue. All surveillance is subsequently lost.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-989328-11&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;11&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;Incident&amp;nbsp;Log-5176-A3-04/05/200█&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;Access&amp;nbsp;Granted&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Log-5176-A3&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;04/05/200█&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;17:57:23&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Immediately following &lt;em&gt;Interview Log-5176-A3&lt;/em&gt;, a mass of anomalous biological material &amp;gt; measuring approximately 260 meters in diameter spontaneously manifested within the interior of Site-██&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-989328-12&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;. Following the manifestation, ██ &amp;gt; Foundation casualties were recorded along with 22 other civilian casualties and numerous injuries. &amp;gt; The material itself, hereby referred to as SCP-5176-3, was entirely inert, presumably having been killed in the event. The material manifested within the matter of the facility, causing massive structural failure. SCP-5176-3 resembles a severed tentacle composed of millions of individual inert SCP-5176 instances. Its mass is in excess of 25,000 metric tons. Analysis of 5176-3&#039;s biochemistry reveals high levels of aluminum and aluminum amalgam.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The manifestation zone has been hypothesized to be limited by the range of the full-phase ██████ &amp;gt; generator. No further experimentation with SCP-5176-1&#039;s reaction to full-phase DPK fields is recommended. In addition, further legislation regarding the use of full-phase ██████ generators in general is advised.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Instances of SCP-5176 and 5176-1 continue to manifest in the environment, indicating that SCP-5176-3 was only a portion of the active anomaly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Head Researcher Dr. Reese Chambers was among the deceased. Dr. ████ ████████ has been chosen as a replacement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dr. Edmund&#039;s behavior has warranted a posthumous reprimand from the Site-██ Director.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

